/**

\page tarch_plotting Plotting

The classes in `tarch/plotter` write unstructured meshes and their fields.
A caller acquires a piece, fills its point coordinates, connectivity and
named fields, then asks the file writer to write the snapshot.


## File writers and time series

The plotting is split into two responsibilities. The actual data of one
snapshot is written through a concrete subclass of the abstract
tarch::plotter::FileWriter. Peano ships VTU (tarch::plotter::VTUFileWriter),
VTKHDF (tarch::plotter::VTKHDFFileWriter), HDF5
(tarch::plotter::HDF5FileWriter) and NetCDF (tarch::plotter::NetCDFFileWriter)
implementations. A file writer receives an output directory. `acquirePiece()`
allocates an ordered piece, and `getPieceBuffers()` returns the buffers of the
points, the cells and the fields of that piece.

The bookkeeping over all snapshots, i.e. the index file that ties the
individual snapshots into one time series, is written separately by a subclass
of tarch::plotter::TimeSeriesWriter. VTU uses
tarch::plotter::PVDTimeSeriesWriter, HDF5 uses
tarch::plotter::XDMFTimeSeriesWriter, and NetCDF uses
tarch::plotter::JSONTimeSeriesWriter. VTKHDF keeps its time steps in one file.

tarch::plotter::createFileWriter() creates the file writer for a format.
tarch::plotter::createTimeSeriesWriter() creates its time-series writer;
`writeSnapshotFile()` writes and registers a snapshot, and
`writeTimeSeriesMetaFile()` writes the index.


## Parallel plotting

The concrete file writer owns the MPI coordination for a snapshot. VTU writes
one `.vtu` file per rank and a global `.pvtu` descriptor; collective HDF5 and
NetCDF writers agree on a field schema, including on empty ranks. Time-series
metadata is written by the global master where the format requires it.


*/
